---
import Marketing from '../layouts/Marketing.astro';
---

<Marketing
  title="Grossline — the monthly report"
  description="What's in the Grossline monthly report: the headline, whether your ads paid off, where your money went, where the platforms disagree with your store, what changed, and the few things worth doing."
  path="/the-report"
>
  <div class="pagehead">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">The monthly report</div>
      <h1>Three pages. The same shape <em>every month</em>.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        So you always know where to look without reading the whole thing. Same order, same
        language, month after month — consistency is the product.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section style="padding-top:56px">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">Every report, in order</div>
      <h2>What's on the page.</h2>
      <div class="cols">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>The headline</h3>
          <p>
            One sentence: whether the month worked, what you kept, and which way things are heading.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Whether your ads paid off</h3>
          <p>
            For every $1 you spent on ads, how many dollars came back — against the point where you
            break even, and against what a new customer costs you.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Where your money went</h3>
          <p>
            From sales at the top down to what you actually kept, line by line — with a note on any
            cost we couldn't see yet.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Where the platforms disagree with your store</h3>
          <p>
            What each ad platform claims it delivered, next to what your store actually recorded.
            Shown as something to be aware of, not something to correct.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>What changed</h3>
          <p>
            Against last month and against this time last year, on the numbers that matter — left out
            where the history doesn't exist yet.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>What to do, and what we'll check</h3>
          <p>
            Up to three specific things worth doing, each with the money at stake — plus what we'll
            check next month, and how last month's turned out.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">Read a real one</div>
      <h2>The whole product, on one page.</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        This sample is made by the same pipeline your report would be — so if you read it, you
        understand exactly what you'd get.
      </p>
      <a href="/sample-report.pdf" class="report-shot" aria-label="Open the sample report PDF">
        <img
          src="/sample-report.png"
          width="820"
          height="1104"
          loading="lazy"
          alt="A full Grossline monthly report for a demo store: the headline, whether the ads paid off, where the money went, where the platforms disagree with the store, what changed, and the findings."
        />
      </a>
      <p style="margin-top:20px">
        <a class="btn" href="/sample-report.pdf">Download the sample report (PDF)</a>
      </p>
      <p class="demo-note">
        Made from a demo store with realistic sample data — not a real merchant's numbers.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Marketing>

<style>
  .report-shot {
    display: block;
    max-width: 40rem;
    margin: 30px 0 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--gl-line);
    border-radius: 14px;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: var(--gl-shadow-image);
  }
  .report-shot img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }
</style>
